# Who can approve a change, and who can land it.
#
# Both powers belong to the people named here and to nobody else. GitHub does
# not count an approving review from anyone without write access, the branch
# rule on `main` requires the approval to come from an owner in this file, and
# it restricts merging to the same accounts. This repository is private, so a
# passer-by cannot open a pull request against it at all; the file stays
# because the same rule is what keeps a stray approval from merging.
#
# Nobody can approve their own pull request, so this list needs enough people
# that work does not stall when one of them is away.
#
# Adding a name here grants both powers. Add people who know this codebase well
# enough to say no.

